  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions where (2S,3S,4R)-10-De-O-Carbamoyl-12-O-Carbamoyl Streptothricin E acts as a target for multiple compounds that ultimately lead to the inhibition of Riboflavin synthase. This compound is linked to PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2, which is targeted by (11C)guanidine, 1-Nonen-3-ol, 3-acetate, and Physalin I. These compounds collectively inhibit Riboflavin synthase, indicating that the target enzyme is a critical node in the pathway. The high scores across all three paths suggest a strong and consistent relationship, but the exact mechanism by which these compounds interact with CDC2L2 and subsequently affect Riboflavin synthase remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential regulatory role of CDC2L2 in the metabolic pathway, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise molecular interactions involved.",
